.SS "\fBp8est_connectivity_t\fP* p8est_connectivity_bcast (\fBp8est_connectivity_t\fP * conn_in, int root, sc_MPI_Comm comm)"

.PP
Broadcast a connectivity structure that exists only on one process to all\&. On the other processors, it will be allocated using p8est_connectivity_new and received\&. This function is collective over the communicator passed\&.
.PP
This function may be called with a communicator that contains only one rank of every shared memory node in preparation to subsequently calling \fBp8est_connectivity_share\fP with an intranode communicator\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIconn_in\fP For the root process the connectivity to be broadcast, for the other processes it must be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIroot\fP The rank of the process that provides the connectivity\&. 
.br
\fIcomm\fP The MPI communicator\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
For the root process this is a pointer to \fIconn_in\fP\&. Else, a pointer to a newly allocated connectivity structure with the same values as \fIconn_in\fP on the root process\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_connectivity_complete (\fBp8est_connectivity_t\fP * conn)"

.PP
Internally connect a connectivity based on tree_to_vertex information\&. Periodicity that is not inherent in the list of vertices will be lost\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIconn\fP The connectivity needs to have proper vertices and tree_to_vertex fields\&. The tree_to_tree and tree_to_face fields must be allocated and satisfy p8est_connectivity_is_valid (conn) but will be overwritten\&. The edge and corner fields will be freed and allocated anew\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_connectivity_coordinates_canonicalize (\fBp8est_connectivity_t\fP * conn, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP treeid, const \fBp4est_qcoord_t\fP coords[], \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP * treeid_out, \fBp4est_qcoord_t\fP coords_out[])"

.PP
Determine the owning tree for a coordinate and transform it there\&. On a boundary between trees, different coordinate systems meet\&. A coordinate on a tree boundary face, edge, or corner generated from the perspective of a specific tree may be transformed into any other touching tree's coordinate system and still refer to the same point in the mesh\&.
.PP
To uniquely identify a coordinate, this function identifies the lowest numbered tree touching this coordinate and transforms the coordinate into that system\&. The result can be used e\&. g\&. in topology hash tables\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIconn\fP A valid connectivity\&. 
.br
\fItreeid\fP The original tree index for this coordinate tuple\&. 
.br
\fIcoords\fP A valid coordinate 2-tuple relative to \fItreeid\fP\&. 
.br
\fItreeid_out\fP The lowest tree index touching the coordinate\&. 
.br
\fIcoords_out\fP The input coordinates, if necessary after transformation into the system of the lowest numbered tree, returned in \fItreeid_out\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

