.SS "void p8est_expand_face_transform (int iface, int nface, int ftransform[])"

.PP
Fill an array with the axis combination of a face neighbor transform\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIiface\fP The number of the originating face\&. 
.br
\fInface\fP Encoded as nface = r * 6 + nf, where nf = 0\&.\&.5 is the neigbbor's connecting face number and r = 0\&.\&.3 is the relative orientation to the neighbor's face\&. This encoding matches p8est_connectivity_t\&. 
.br
\fIftransform\fP This array holds 9 integers\&. [0]\&.\&.[2] The coordinate axis sequence of the origin face, the first two referring to the tangentials and the third to the normal\&. A permutation of (0, 1, 2)\&. [3]\&.\&.[5] The coordinate axis sequence of the target face\&. [6]\&.\&.[8] Edge reversal flags for tangential axes (boolean); face code in [0, 3] for the normal coordinate q: 0: q' = -q 1: q' = q + 1 2: q' = q - 1 3: q' = 2 - q 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_find_corner_transform (\fBp8est_connectivity_t\fP * connectivity, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP itree, int icorner, \fBp8est_corner_info_t\fP * ci)"

